{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Research record for this epic (experiments on origin/main 083620b0; venv Python 3.12, mcp 1.29.0, pydantic 2.13.4; prototypes ran against a `git archive origin/main` export because the local editable install trails main).\n\nCorrections to the original brief, verified: `check_mcp_models.py` is `src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py` (174 LOC; CI step `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:765-773`; `pyproject.toml:583`); the coverage test is `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py` (396 LOC). The 21 `mcp_server.py` re-exports are already gone (commit e5bda753); the residue is `tests/interfaces/facades/test_internal_shim_removal_e54e_heldout.py:39-46`, which still imports `_mcp_models`. 13 tools (not 16) lack an `outputSchema`: `audit_trail, bridge_projects_list, explain_criterion, reopen_ticket, review_code, review_plan, review_plan_start, run_workflow, scan_spec, sign_review, transition_ticket, verify_completion, verify_completion_start`; 16 is the `mcp_only` count. `tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py` is 486 LOC. `tool_annotation_presets()` lives in `_mcp_models.py:585-619` and is imported by all three registrars; deleting the module rehomes it (into `_mcp_schema.py`).\n\nExperiment 1 (annotation census over `rebar.__all__` with `inspect.signature`): 61 functions, 84 unannotated params (61 `repo_root=None` plus 23 others); the full annotation table is the annotation story's description. `scripts/gen_api_surface.py:93-108` records only `[name, kind, default]` plus the return annotation, so `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` does not change. 30 of 34 return annotations name `rebar.types` TypedDicts imported only under `TYPE_CHECKING`, so `inspect.signature(fn, eval_str=True)` raises `NameError`; the derivation factory resolves hints itself.\n\nExperiment 2 (32 pydantic models vs `schemas/*.json`): 20 mapped, 12 unmapped; 20 invented nullabilities, 11 dropped enums, 5 relaxed required sets, 2 `additionalProperties` disagreements; the itemised amendment list is the schema story's first comment. Wire measurement over a real `build_server().call_tool`: `show_ticket` 44 keys / 12 nulls on the wire vs 36 / 6 from the library; write acks carry five `push_status` nulls where the library returns `{\"state\":\"ok\"}`. Decision: emit exactly what the library returns; absent stays absent (the rule bug 3a02 already applied to 15 properties); the SDK validates `structuredContent` against the advertised schema at call time so a non-null-typed field must be absent, not null. Mechanism proven by prototype: `-> dict[str, Any]` gets a pass-through `RootModel`, `-> list[dict[str, Any]]` wraps as `{\"result\": [...]}`, and setting `fn_metadata.output_schema` to an inlined canonical schema makes `list_tools()` advertise it and the lowlevel validator accept absent optionals; inlining is mandatory because `jsonschema.validate` cannot resolve cross-file `$ref`s.\n\nExperiment 3 (48 library-backed tools: 26 read, 22 write): 0 of 48 descriptions equal the library docstring; beyond `repo_root` stripping and the 10 manifest-declared divergences, eight input contracts differ (`list_tickets.full/priority`, `bridge_run.profile`, `set_file_impact.impact`, `set_verify_commands.commands`, `sign_manifest.manifest`, `attach_commits.commits`, `summary.ticket_ids`, `transition_ticket` order); all are transport policy and live in the override table (derivation story, first comment).\n\nChild stories created (chain S1 -> S2 -> S3):\n- S1 bossy-poetic-polliwog (18f1-f25d-0337-4a06): annotate the 84 library parameters.\n- S2 quilted-nepotic-kitty (9835-95f2-3072-4dc1): canonical outputSchemas, delete the pydantic mirror and drift gate, release note; depends on S1.\n- S3 masonic-excusable-guppy (c296-4bc7-26be-489d): derive the 48 tools, delete the parity gate, ADR 0118; depends on S2.\n\nCross-epic: S2 loads `plan_review_status.schema.json` as-is (its enum edits belong to the LLM-leftovers epic winded-chunky-sheldrake); no other epic edits `_mcp_*.py`. Baseline maintenance: S2 removes a `ci_gate` workflow step and S3 removes `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`, so each runs `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in its change (operator-sanctioned; precedent commit 81da792)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788806978161291304,"uuid":"96f9c593-a34d-4f57-a29f-a739069befd6"}